.TH BREATHGSLB-LICENSECTL 8 "September 2026" "BreathGSLB" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
breathgslb-licensectl \- list, revoke and regenerate BreathGSLB license keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B breathgslb-licensectl
.B \-db
.I path
.RB [ list | revoke
.IR key |
.B regen
.IR key ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B breathgslb-licensectl
is the operator utility for managing the license keys stored in a
BreathGSLB sqlite license database. It operates directly on the
database file: stop the daemon, or at least ensure no concurrent
writer, before mutating keys.
.TP
.B list
Print one line per license showing the account email, the key, the
support expiry date and the support level. The data comes from joining
the
.I licenses
and
.I users
tables.
.TP
.BI "revoke " key
Delete the license row holding
.IR key .
Exits non-zero with
.I "revoke: no such key"
when nothing was deleted.
.TP
.BI "regen " key
Replace
.I key
with a freshly generated 32-character key, print the new key on
stdout, and exit non-zero with
.I "regen: no such key"
when the old key does not exist. Hand the printed key to the licensee;
the encrypted payload stays valid because only the wrapping key
changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-db " path
Path to the sqlite database file. Required; there is no default.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success. Any usage error, missing key, or database failure exits
non-zero with the reason on stderr (Go
.IR log.Fatal ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/breathgslb/
Configuration and state directory. The license database path is a
deployment choice; pass it with
.BR \-db .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR breathgslb (8),
.BR breathgslb-licensegen (8),
.BR breathgslb.conf (5)
